    "question": {
      ":question/id": "87e7e8ce-2345-5d9c-b079-011b3688619d",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -5 & -9 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & 25 & 21 \\\\ -16 & -5 & 6 & 18 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -9 & -16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations\n\n- $C_{1}:=C_{1}+2C_{2}$\n- $C_{3}:=\\ldots$\n- $C_{4}:=\\ldots$\n\neach of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 4 other than $a_{42}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -5 & -9 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}+2C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & -5 & -9 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-3C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & 25 & 7 \\\\ -16 & -5 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{4}:=C_{4}-2C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & 25 & 21 \\\\ -16 & -5 & 6 & 18 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -9 & -16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{3}:=C_{3}-3C_{2}$ and $C_{4}:=C_{4}-2C_{2}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "dee57f18-cde0-5f86-858d-4fe921deb046",
