    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b050c383-5ac4-5188-8bfa-e12e4c47caad",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -10 & 10 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -7 & -5 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-13 & 17 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -29 & 32 & 5 & 13 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations\n\n- $C_{1}:=\\ldots$\n- $C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{3}$\n- $C_{4}:=\\ldots$\n\neach of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 2 other than $a_{23}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -10 & 10 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -7 & -5 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-5C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-13 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 10 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -29 & 7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -5 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-13 & 17 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -29 & 32 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{4}:=C_{4}+2C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-13 & 17 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -29 & 32 & 5 & 13 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{1}:=C_{1}-5C_{3}$ and $C_{4}:=C_{4}+2C_{3}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
